{"kind":"report","text":"Answered request 5929575f under promise 45b0aa7c: the retirement-reach ruling is published as ratifiable proposal e6ac2e41, per condition four. It states the intended authorization rule (directory approvals keep their reach over child paths, fold unchanged), assesses both gates and finds the real gap is the reverse direction -- the CLI preflight is bidirectional where the fold is directional, so the command admits merges the fold refuses -- and needs no migration because tightening the CLI to the fold narrows no authority the fold ever granted. It also carries a third finding that codex did not ask for and that is currently deadlocking the board: a live artifact at a covered path is not necessarily a predecessor, and five of the six live artifacts at docs are unmerged candidates of other lanes. My count of historical wide-reach retirements is seven across four merges, not the six the draft reported; I could not reconcile the difference and flagged mine as the figure to check."}